This is part of why PCR interests me--because it resembles a
psychological realization I had a few years ago that did me a
lot of good.

The realization was that I don't have to follow up thoughts.
Just because a thought or question comes into my head, I don't
have to follow the implications or answer the question.  In
fact, it was a shock to me to realize that just because I
think something, I don't have to consider myself to *believe*
it.

I'm talking psychology here, not philosophy.  It's about what I
do with my brain from moment to moment, and the fact that it's
under my control--at least more than I had realized it was.

I wouldn't have described myself as "obsessed," by the way.
In retrospect, it was more like "caught in some bad 
assumptions."  Some amazingly tricky and unconscious 
assumptions about, e.g., what one "must" think if one thinks 
so-and-so...

I guess the amazing thing is how freeing those couple trivial-
seeming ideas could be.

Anyway, PCR *resembles* that, so to me it has the smell of a 
good idea.  It's a very different smell from most ideas, and
I'm always curious whether other people have found themselves
trapped--or released--in ways like I did.

